==========================================================================
PART 2 -- THE SHARPER PREDICTION: r_M IS NOT FREE
==========================================================================
  From Sigma_ph = a_0/(pi G) = const and M_ph(<r_M) = M_b:
      M_b = (a_0/G) r_M^2     ->   r_M = sqrt(G M_b / a_0)
    M_b = 1e+09: r_M =   1.220 kpc, r_cap = r_M (a_0/g_ext) =   0.718 kpc
    M_b = 1e+11: r_M =  12.203 kpc, r_cap = r_M (a_0/g_ext) =   7.178 kpc
  [PASS] L3 [THE PREDICTION] the halo's physical extent is
      r_cap = (a_0/g_ext) sqrt(G M_b/a_0) -- fixed by the baryon mass
      and the environment, with no free length scale
         measured: r_cap = (a_0/g_ext) sqrt(G M_b/a_0); e.g. M_b=1e11 -> 7.18 kpc
         Testable: halo size vs baryon mass and environment. The EFE cap and
         the amplitude law together give a definite size, not a fit.

